            <title><![CDATA[ChatGPT for SNES (109 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://www.bxfoundry.com/chatgpt_snes/</link>
            <guid>50568548</guid>
            <pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:25:59 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.bxfoundry.com/chatgpt_snes/">https://www.bxfoundry.com/chatgpt_snes/</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50568548">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div>
    <div>
      <p><span>ChatGPT for SNES</span></p>
      <div id="screen">
          <p><img src="https://www.bxfoundry.com/chatgpt_snes/img/title.png" width="256" height="224" alt="The game's title screen"></p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p>ChatGPT for SNES can make mistakes.</p>
    
    <div>
      <p><span><b>Type on your keyboard. Enter sends.</b> Backspace deletes; Page Up and Page Down scroll. It simulates a control pad entry.</span><span><b>Your keys are the controller:</b> arrows, X = A, Z = B, A = Y, Enter = Start.</span></p>
      <p><b>Your keys are the controller:</b> arrows, X = A, Z = B, A = Y, Enter = Start.</p>
      </div>
    <p>
      <small>Letters move the cursor on the game's keyboard and type. Enter sends. The touch buttons work too (B deletes).</small>
    </p>
  </div><div>
    <p><a href="https://www.bxfoundry.com/chatgpt_snes/rom/ver_v07_pure.zip" download="ChatGPT_for_SNES_v0.7_pure.zip">Download the v0.7 ROM</a> (1.5&nbsp;MB zip: one .sfc file).
      Requires a flash cart with Super FX support, such as an FXPak Pro or an sd2snes with current firmware. Leave Chip Options › SuperFX speed at Normal.
      <a href="https://www.bxfoundry.com/chatgpt_snes/rom/ver_v07.zip" download="ChatGPT_for_SNES_v0.7_fact_book.zip">The build with the fact book</a> (17&nbsp;MB zip: the .sfc and its .msu file) also needs MSU-1 support: put both files in the same folder with their names unchanged.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>ChatGPT for SNES is an unofficial experiment designed by Benj Edwards and coded by AI agents: a ChatGPT-style chat program for the Super Nintendo. Its training conversations were written by gpt-oss-120b, OpenAI's open-weight model. Not made or endorsed by OpenAI.</li>
      <li>This is version 0.7 (2 November 2026).</li>
      <li>A small language model with about 2.2 million parameters runs on the cartridge's Super FX 2 chip and writes its answers one word at a time.</li>
      <li>In the main build every word it writes comes from the language model. A second build adds a fact book (the opening sentences of 150,000 Simple English Wikipedia articles, stored in the cartridge's MSU-1 data file): like ChatGPT searching the web, its model can decide to look something up and print what the book says.</li>
      <li>Here it runs in the Snes9x emulator in your browser; the first visit loads about 4&nbsp;MB (19&nbsp;MB with the fact book).</li>
      <li>Press Start (Enter) on the title screen, then type on your keyboard and press Enter to send. Each letter takes a moment to appear, because the page moves the cursor on the game's own on-screen keyboard.</li>
      <li>It is not a useful assistant: the model is millions of times smaller than the models behind ChatGPT, knows about 8,000 words, and often gets things wrong, sometimes confidently. The fact book can carry mistakes too.</li>
    </ul>
    <section aria-labelledby="h-hw">
      <h2 id="h-hw">On a real Super NES</h2>
      <figure>
        <img src="https://www.bxfoundry.com/chatgpt_snes/img/hw_setup.jpg" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" alt="A Super Nintendo with a flash cartridge, connected to a small white JVC CRT TV showing the ChatGPT for SNES title screen, next to a lamp with three glowing globes.">
        <figcaption>ChatGPT for SNES on a Super Nintendo and a CRT TV, running from an sd2snes flash cart.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="https://www.bxfoundry.com/chatgpt_snes/img/hw_chat.jpg" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" alt="The CRT TV showing a chat. ChatGPT for SNES says it is a tiny AI that lives inside a Super Nintendo; asked &quot;who is mario&quot;, it answers that Mario is a small plumber who jumps and saves a Princess.">
        <figcaption>A chat on the same TV.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <p>If you liked this, you might enjoy <a href="https://www.bxfoundry.com/seance_nes/">Séance</a>, which runs a tiny AI language model on a real NES.</p>
  </div></div>]]></description>
        </item>
