<p><strong>Mitigation</strong></p>

<p>Deactivate the OAuth Service package.</p>

<p><strong>Detail</strong></p>

<ul>
<li>CVE-2026-120382

<ul>
<li>Severity: Critical</li>
<li>CVSS3 Base Score: 9.8</li>
<li>CVSS3 Vector: <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.1#CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H">CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H</a></li>
<li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/88.html">CWE-88: Improper Neutralization of Argument Delimiters in a Command</a></li>
<li>An improper neutralization of argument delimiters in a command vulnerability in the OAuth API in Synology DiskStation Manager (DSM) before 6.2.4-25556-9, 7.1.1-42962-10, 7.2.1-69057-14, 7.2.2-72806-11, 7.3.2-86009-6, and 7.4.1-90080-2 allows remote attackers to read or write arbitrary files and conduct denial-of-service attacks.</li>
</ul></li>
</ul>

