            <title><![CDATA[Rebuilding my local voice assistant pipeline (114 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://blog.platypush.tech/article/Rewriting-my-voice-assistant-pipeline</link>
            <guid>50566261</guid>
            <pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:57:14 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://blog.platypush.tech/article/Rewriting-my-voice-assistant-pipeline">https://blog.platypush.tech/article/Rewriting-my-voice-assistant-pipeline</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50566261">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div>


      <div>
<ul>
<li><a href="#wake-word-detection-a-new-assistantmicrowakeword-plugin">Wake word detection: a new assistant.microwakeword plugin</a></li>
<li><a href="#speech-to-text-assistantopenai-with-a-much-better-ear">Speech-to-text: assistant.openai, with a much better ear</a></li>
<li><a href="#responses-and-context-the-openai-plugin">Responses and context: the openai plugin</a></li>
<li><a href="#text-to-speech-ttsopenai">Text-to-speech: tts.openai</a></li>
<li><a href="#the-full-configuration">The full configuration</a></li>
<li><a href="#what-changed-on-the-code-side">What changed on the code side</a></li>
<li><a href="#caveats">Caveats</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
<p>I <a href="https://blog.platypush.tech/article/Local-voice-assistant">wrote an article</a> a couple of months ago describing how I rebuilt my old voice assistant pipeline in <a href="https://platypush.tech/">Platypush</a>.</p>
<p>And I wrote earlier articles describing my journey through self-hosted voice assistants - <a href="https://blog.platypush.tech/article/The-state-of-voice-assistant-integrations-in-2024">in 2024</a> (with <a href="https://picovoice.ai/">Picovoice</a>), <a href="https://blog.platypush.tech/article/Build-custom-voice-assistants">in 2020</a> (diving into the legacy <a href="https://docs.platypush.tech/platypush/plugins/assistant.google.html"><code>assistant.google</code></a> integration, the now defunct <code>assistant.alexa</code> integration, the now defunct Snowboy integration, the now defunct DeepSpeech integration and Picovoice) and the <a href="https://blog.platypush.tech/article/Build-your-customizable-voice-assistant-with-Platypush">original article in 2019</a> describing the Google Assistant integration.</p>
<p>For a couple of months I used the voice pipeline described in my latest article as my main driver, but after getting used to the robustness of commercial voice assistants I was unhappy with the high rates of false positives/negatives of my self-hosted pipeline, as well as its lack of robustness in detecting start/end of speech, especially in noisy environments and using cheap microphones.</p>
<p>After a bit of experimentation, I decided to swap and fine tune a few parts, and after a couple of days of trying the results are satisfying enough for me to write a short article about it.</p>
<p>The resulting pipeline is:</p>
